{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall destroy their name, etc.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said (Avodah Zarah 45a): ״What does this come to teach us? Has it not already been said: ׳אַבֵּד תְּאַבְּדוּן׳?״ And they said that it comes to say that one must root out the roots of the asherah, and Rabbi Akiva said that it comes to say to change its name to one of disgrace — end of quote. Or perhaps the verse comes to give a special warning regarding the land of Israel distinct from all other lands, in the manner that the Rambam wrote: concerning other lands, even though we are obligated to destroy idolatry, we are not required to search after it to destroy it — whereas in the land of Israel one must search after it to destroy it throughout all our land — end of quote. And this is what the verse precisely means: <b>and you shall destroy their name from that place</b> — which is the holy land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:50.155859054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}